4 The National Company Law Tribunal ("NCLT") vide its order dated August 07, 2025, has sanctioned the scheme of Arrangement ("Scheme") for transfer and vesting of "the Advanced Material Undertaking" of the Company to Arvind Advanced Materials Limited ("AAML"), a wholly owned subsidiary of the Company, on a going concern basis by way of slump sale with effect from the appointed date i.e. April 01, 2024 under sections 230 to 232 and other applicable provisions of the Companies Act, 2013.  &lt;BR&gt; 
 &lt;BR&gt; 
The certified copy of the said order was filed with the Registrar of Companies on September 1, 2025 ("Effective Date"). Accordingly, all assets and liabilities as at the Appointed Date related to the Advanced Materials Undertaking are transferred from Arvind Limited on the Effective Date. Accordingly, the post-tax profit pertaining related to the Advanced Materials Undertaking has been presented as a discontinued operation (including re-presenting the same for the prior periods presented) in the standalone financial results in accordance with Ind AS 105.  &lt;BR&gt; 
