6 Pursuant to the amendments in the Finance (No. 2) Act 2024, long term capital gains tax rate was changed from 20% plus surcharge and cess (with indexation) to 12. 5% plus surcharge and cess (without indexation). In accordance with the said amendments, the deferred tax asset has been reduced by Rs 56. 77 crores in  &lt;BR&gt; 
previous financial year. It is to be noted that only a provision is being made in the books of accounts to record the Deferred Tax in line with the applicable accounting standards and recently enacted tax rate change.  &lt;BR&gt; 
